Everything is working now.

**What was wrong:** Your `pip` installation was corrupted — the `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata folder existed in `site-packages`, but the actual `pip/` package directory (the Python code) was missing. This made `pip3` crash with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'` because the wrapper script could find its entry point but there was nothing to import.

**What I did:** Removed the stale `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` directory, then ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade` which extracted pip from the bundled wheel (`/usr/local/lib/python3.13/ensurepip/_bundled/pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl`). Pip is now fully functional.

